                "tldr": "In this paper, the authors present an ethnographic evidence of inmate experiences with direct supervision at Douglas County Department of Corrections in Omaha, Nebraska (USA) and find that inmates generally do feel safe in this jail environment, for a combination of reasons, some of which are related to spatial design.",
                "podcast": null,
                "podcast_generation_allowed": true,
                "entity_type": "PAPER",
                "score": 0.6793707,
                "section_names": [
                    "Discussion"
                ],
                "rank": 15,
                "relevance_data": {},
                "source": "scispace_full_text",
                "relevance_summary": "Uses spatial design analysis to link environment perception with violence; provides self\u2011reported assault rates versus official data; mentions inmate\u2011staff conflict but lacks guard stress or program details.",
                "relevance_metadata": {
                    "criteria_judgments": [
