                "tldr": "This paper developed the communicative theory of learning how to teach, a grounded theory based on communicative messages of the Department of Corrections officers and Bureau of Land Manager employees who work with inmates in a western state Wild Horse Inmate Program.",
                "podcast": null,
                "podcast_generation_allowed": true,
                "entity_type": "PAPER",
                "score": 0.65146625,
                "section_names": [
                    "Correctional Officers"
                ],
                "rank": 19,
                "relevance_data": {},
                "source": "scispace_full_text",
                "relevance_summary": "Uses RPB training to improve officer\u2011inmate relations and rehabilitation outcomes; details officer identity, masculinity, and coercion; cites surveys on brutality but lacks concrete violence metrics; mentions stress\u2011related identity tensions; references abuse narratives without rights\u2011focused analysis; omits facility conditions, legal analysis, and comparative history.",
                "relevance_metadata": {
